 "identifier": "kaal:claim:2831040-003",
 "text": "Regulators face a two ended timing trap: at the early stage of an innovation they lack information about its possible impact, and at the later stage the innovation is entrenched, so regulatory change becomes far more costly for innovating corporations.",
